00:20:45.214 --> 00:20:47.030
there were these British soldier group

518
00:20:47.030 --> 00:20:48.730
called the Black and Tans,

519
00:20:48.730 --> 00:20:49.720
and they came to Ireland,

520
00:20:49.720 --> 00:20:52.170
and they massacred a bunch of people and stuff like that.

521
00:20:52.170 --> 00:20:54.300
So when they're calling you Black,

522
00:20:54.300 --> 00:20:56.350
they're calling you one of those Black and Tans,

523
00:20:56.350 --> 00:20:58.734
like, so I was pushed around at school

524
00:20:58.734 --> 00:21:02.170
because of that kinda stuff, so I think when I was,

525
00:21:02.170 --> 00:21:05.433
when I was little and I had no confidence or no courage,

526
00:21:05.433 --> 00:21:08.630
it, you know, that affected me.

527
00:21:08.630 --> 00:21:10.510
And then after I started drinking,

528
00:21:10.510 --> 00:21:13.850
and I had this psychological change

529
00:21:13.850 --> 00:21:15.670
made me a different person,

530
00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:18.700
then I was like determined not to take any shit from anybody

531
00:21:18.700 --> 00:21:21.000
because of how I had been treated when I was younger,

532
00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:21.833
you know?

533
00:21:22.700 --> 00:21:24.430
Yeah, so I think I probably had a little bit of a,

534
00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:27.360
it took a, it took a while for that to grow, you know?

535
00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:29.715
Like even when I first started drinking,

536
00:21:29.715 --> 00:21:32.270
I don't know what it's like now,

537
00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:34.900
but when I was growing up back home,

538
00:21:34.900 --> 00:21:37.790
Ireland was like violent, you know.

539
00:21:37.790 --> 00:21:39.910
Not a lot of people getting murdered,

540
00:21:39.910 --> 00:21:43.900
but when you go out drinking, everybody used to drink a lot.

541
00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:45.350
And then at the end of the night,

542
00:21:45.350 --> 00:21:47.810
we would go to these fast food restaurants.

543
00:21:47.810 --> 00:21:49.680
They call them chippers back home

544
00:21:49.680 --> 00:21:52.769
cause they sell fries.

545
00:21:52.769 --> 00:21:53.776
Yeah.

546
00:21:53.776 --> 00:21:54.609
Like fish and chips, you know?

547
00:21:54.609 --> 00:21:56.700
And after the night of drinking,

548
00:21:56.700 --> 00:21:58.070
everybody goes to the chipper,

549
00:21:58.070 --> 00:22:00.894
and that's when you would see the fights, you know?

550
00:22:00.894 --> 00:22:01.892
Cause you have.

551
00:22:01.892 --> 00:22:02.897
It's like sport.

552
00:22:02.897 --> 00:22:03.730
It's like a spectator sport though.

553
00:22:03.730 --> 00:22:04.629
Oh, absolutely, yeah.

554
00:22:04.629 --> 00:22:05.462
And I used to sit in the chipper

555
00:22:05.462 --> 00:22:09.079
and watch these fucking boys trolling each other,

556
00:22:09.079 --> 00:22:10.590
beating each other.

557
00:22:10.590 --> 00:22:12.740
It was, it was mayhem.

558
00:22:12.740 --> 00:22:15.240
And when I was like, when I first came to America,

559
00:22:15.240 --> 00:22:16.780
I was only 160 pounds.

560
00:22:16.780 --> 00:22:18.270
I was light, you know?

561
00:22:18.270 --> 00:22:20.780
So back then I was like a skinny, light kid,

562
00:22:20.780 --> 00:22:22.860
but I'm like taking all this shit in,

563
00:22:22.860 --> 00:22:25.600
and it was kind of, it was really exciting.

564
00:22:25.600 --> 00:22:27.660
It was like an action movie in front of you.

565
00:22:27.660 --> 00:22:29.112
Yeah.

566
00:22:29.112 --> 00:22:29.945
You know? And it was funny.

567
00:22:29.945 --> 00:22:31.672
Sometimes it was like,

568
00:22:31.672 --> 00:22:34.620
sometimes it would be over nothing.

569
00:22:34.620 --> 00:22:37.280
Like say you're in the chipper,

570
00:22:37.280 --> 00:22:38.960
and there's a guy there with his woman,

571
00:22:38.960 --> 00:22:42.680
and a drunk guy like gives her the eye.

572
00:22:42.680 --> 00:22:44.610
He could get knocked out for that, you know?

573
00:22:44.610 --> 00:22:46.690
Or he spills some chips on somebody.

574
00:22:46.690 --> 00:22:49.280
You'd see them flying over tables.

575
00:22:49.280 --> 00:22:52.470
It reminds me of that scene in "The Gentleman."

576
00:22:52.470 --> 00:22:53.992
You see that movie?

577
00:22:53.992 --> 00:22:56.100
Where Colin Farrell beats the shit of out of a bunch of kids

578
00:22:56.100 --> 00:22:58.800
in a chipper, you know, that idea.

579
00:22:58.800 --> 00:23:00.310
Yeah, that could happen anytime.

580
00:23:00.310 --> 00:23:03.990
But, and when I first started going out,

581
00:23:03.990 --> 00:23:06.060
I used to work at a gas station.

582
00:23:06.060 --> 00:23:07.170
Back in the day,

583
00:23:07.170 --> 00:23:10.130
there was people called gas station attendants

584
00:23:10.130 --> 00:23:12.080
who would come and fill your gas for you.

585
00:23:12.080 --> 00:23:15.780
Like now everybody just, everybody fills their own gas.

586
00:23:15.780 --> 00:23:17.440
But that was my first job.

587
00:23:17.440 --> 00:23:18.437
I was like 15 or 16.

588
00:23:18.437 --> 00:23:20.780
And I was working with these older boys.

589
00:23:20.780 --> 00:23:23.137
And one of them, I probably shouldn't say his name,

590
00:23:23.137 --> 00:23:24.670
but his nickname was Tits

591
00:23:24.670 --> 00:23:27.530
cause he had man boobs, you know,

592
00:23:27.530 --> 00:23:31.050
but Tits used to bring me out, and I used to look up to him.

593
00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:33.385
You know, he was one of these guys,

594
00:23:33.385 --> 00:23:37.340
when I first met him, he had been arrested like 30 times

595
00:23:37.340 --> 00:23:40.350
just for like fighting or stupid drunk shit,

596
00:23:40.350 --> 00:23:42.000
and he never went to jail

597
00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:44.324
cause when I was growing up, there was like,

598
00:23:44.324 --> 00:23:45.600
there was no real penalties for that.

599
00:23:45.600 --> 00:23:48.810
Like in California, I couldn't believe when I got here,

600
00:23:48.810 --> 00:23:50.090
there's not a whole lot of fights

601
00:23:50.090 --> 00:23:53.360
because if you like just put your hand on someone

602
00:23:53.360 --> 00:23:55.490
or spit on them, you're going to jail.

603
00:23:55.490 --> 00:23:58.460
But back home you could kick the shit outta someone,

604
00:23:58.460 --> 00:24:01.460
and maybe if the cops got you,

605
00:24:01.460 --> 00:24:03.348
you might have to go to court

606
00:24:03.348 --> 00:24:04.540
and pay a couple of hundred dollars fine.

607
00:24:04.540 --> 00:24:05.373
That's all it was.

608
00:24:05.373 --> 00:24:09.560
There was like a boys will be boys' mentality to the law.

609
00:24:09.560 --> 00:24:10.925
I don't--

610
00:24:10.925 --> 00:24:11.924
Is it still like that there?

611
00:24:11.924 --> 00:24:12.928
I don't know.

612
00:24:12.928 --> 00:24:13.980
It might not be, but when I was growing up,

613
00:24:13.980 --> 00:24:15.848
that's how it was.

614
00:24:15.848 --> 00:24:16.986
Right.

615
00:24:16.986 --> 00:24:18.010
And I used to hang out with Tits, and he'd bring me out,

616
00:24:18.010 --> 00:24:22.320
and you know, he was kind of a role model for me.

617
00:24:22.320 --> 00:24:23.153
Yeah.

618
00:24:23.153 --> 00:24:24.573
You know.

619
00:24:24.573 --> 00:24:27.530
What is the truth or the lived experience

620
00:24:27.530 --> 00:24:30.221
of growing up around the IRA?

621
00:24:30.221 --> 00:24:32.380
Cause I, you know, my relationship to that

622
00:24:32.380 --> 00:24:35.330
is just what I've read in books or seen in movies.

623
00:24:35.330 --> 00:24:37.182
Well, you know what, I'll tell you,

624
00:24:37.182 --> 00:24:38.202
I'll tell you the main thing

625
00:24:38.202 --> 00:24:39.830
that Hollywood never gets right about the IRA.

626
00:24:39.830 --> 00:24:41.940
Like whenever you see the movies or anything like that,

627
00:24:41.940 --> 00:24:46.940
about the IRA, they make it out

628
00:24:47.330 --> 00:24:50.360
like it's this really fucking secret thing

629
00:24:50.360 --> 00:24:52.230
where these guys come out of nowhere,

630
00:24:52.230 --> 00:24:55.890
and nobody knows who they are, but in real life,

631
00:24:55.890 --> 00:24:58.310
you know exactly who's in the IRA.

632
00:24:58.310 --> 00:25:00.670
Cause in Ireland, like it's a small country.

633
00:25:00.670 --> 00:25:02.440
Everybody knows everybody.

634
00:25:02.440 --> 00:25:06.590
So if your neighbor is in the IRA, you know.

635
00:25:06.590 --> 00:25:10.880
Like if their kid is on the team with you,

636
00:25:10.880 --> 00:25:13.904
everybody knows because they have marches and shit,

637
00:25:13.904 --> 00:25:14.737
and you see them at the marches,

638
00:25:14.737 --> 00:25:17.220
or they might come to the bar to collect money

639
00:25:17.220 --> 00:25:19.520
for whatever the prisoners

640
00:25:19.520 --> 00:25:21.640
or whatever the fuck they're collecting money for.

641
00:25:21.640 --> 00:25:25.970
So in real life, everybody knows exactly who's in the IRA.

642
00:25:25.970 --> 00:25:30.908
So there's no secret, you know, but it's still.

643
00:25:30.908 --> 00:25:33.910
And you just sort of tip toe around it and tread lightly.

644
00:25:33.910 --> 00:25:35.530
It depends.

645
00:25:35.530 --> 00:25:37.120
I have a load of friends who were in it

646
00:25:37.120 --> 00:25:39.930
and whose families are in it.

647
00:25:39.930 --> 00:25:42.010
You know, the way it is as well,

648
00:25:42.010 --> 00:25:44.430
it's like a volunteer sort of a thing, so.

649
00:25:44.430 --> 00:25:46.330
They're called volunteers,

650
00:25:46.330 --> 00:25:47.880
so some people join up for awhile,

651
00:25:47.880 --> 00:25:49.370
and then they go away again.

652
00:25:49.370 --> 00:25:51.073
And that's how it is like.

653
00:25:51.930 --> 00:25:52.965
Right.

654
00:25:52.965 --> 00:25:54.400
You know, but I always ended up with being friends

655
00:25:54.400 --> 00:25:56.245
with a bunch of their kids

656
00:25:56.245 --> 00:25:58.270
cause there were a lot of 'em were kinda wild like I was.

657
00:25:58.270 --> 00:25:59.103
You know?

658
00:25:59.103 --> 00:26:00.270
Yeah, wow.

659
00:26:00.270 --> 00:26:02.449
So the drinking starts to escalate.

660
00:26:02.449 --> 00:26:04.420
Hash enters the picture.

661
00:26:04.420 --> 00:26:07.110
At some point you start kind of selling,

662
00:26:07.110 --> 00:26:10.070
dealing a little bit, like walk me through that next phase.

663
00:26:10.070 --> 00:26:12.680
It was the exact same shit as the drinking.

664
00:26:12.680 --> 00:26:14.910
With the drinking, I started selling IDs

665
00:26:14.910 --> 00:26:17.990
to fund my drinking, and then with the hash,

666
00:26:17.990 --> 00:26:20.540
I started, like I felt,

667
00:26:20.540 --> 00:26:23.610
I started smoking hash when I was maybe 16 or 17 too,

668
00:26:23.610 --> 00:26:25.913
and it, cause it was, I knew it couldn't kill you.

669
00:26:25.913 --> 00:26:28.370
And it looked cool, you know?

670
00:26:28.370 --> 00:26:30.837
And I had seen it on TV and movies and stuff like that.

671
00:26:30.837 --> 00:26:33.040
And so I wanted to try it,

672
00:26:33.040 --> 00:26:35.752
and I met these guys one night in Cavan.

673
00:26:35.752 --> 00:26:38.200
Can't really use their names.

674
00:26:38.200 --> 00:26:39.257
Let's call 'em,

675
00:26:40.871 --> 00:26:42.810
this guy has a really obvious name.

676
00:26:42.810 --> 00:26:44.740
We'll call him Pigeon, right?

677
00:26:44.740 --> 00:26:46.165
All right, there you go.

678
00:26:46.165 --> 00:26:48.827
So I met Pigeon and his buddy one night, and he goes,

679
00:26:48.827 --> 00:26:50.770
do you wanna buy some hash, hi?

680
00:26:50.770 --> 00:26:52.510
They have all this funny way of talking.

681
00:26:52.510 --> 00:26:54.249
You think my way is funny.

682
00:26:54.249 --> 00:26:55.500
They have all this weird lingo.

683
00:26:55.500 --> 00:26:58.337
Like where I'm from, they'll say hi, Sham, or hi, Sobla.

684
00:26:58.337 --> 00:26:59.500
They'd say, hi, Sham.

685
00:26:59.500 --> 00:27:01.200
You wanna buy some hash, hi?

686
00:27:01.200 --> 00:27:02.520
They say hi about everything.

687
00:27:02.520 --> 00:27:03.800
It's weird.

688
00:27:03.800 --> 00:27:05.090
So I says, yeah, how much is it?

689
00:27:05.090 --> 00:27:06.790
He goes, I give you a five spot.

690
00:27:06.790 --> 00:27:08.877
It was five pounds at the time.

691
00:27:08.877 --> 00:27:11.530
Now we have euros, but back then we had pounds.

692
00:27:11.530 --> 00:27:13.750
So he like sold me this little ball of hash,

693
00:27:13.750 --> 00:27:15.240
and it was in a matchbox,

694
00:27:15.240 --> 00:27:18.104
and he said, do you know how to smoke it?

695
00:27:18.104 --> 00:27:19.870
I said no.

696
00:27:19.870 --> 00:27:22.870
And he rolled me a joint, and we smoked it together.

697
00:27:22.870 --> 00:27:24.322
And it was like,

698
00:27:24.322 --> 00:27:26.450
it was like discovering alcohol all over again,

699
00:27:26.450 --> 00:27:28.450
Except not so crazy.

700
00:27:28.450 --> 00:27:29.460
It was more chilled.

701
00:27:29.460 --> 00:27:33.040
Like there was no, you wouldn't fall down on hash really.

702
00:27:33.040 --> 00:27:36.628
You probably couldn't crash a car on it, you know?

703
00:27:36.628 --> 00:27:39.110
But once I discovered the hash too,

704
00:27:39.110 --> 00:27:41.350
it was something that I wanted to do all the time,

705
00:27:41.350 --> 00:27:43.400
even though I knew it was illegal.

706
00:27:43.400 --> 00:27:46.440
I had to be careful not to get caught, but yeah.

707
00:27:46.440 --> 00:27:51.440
I started to sell it to fund my use of it.

708
00:27:51.490 --> 00:27:53.850
Yeah, and what's going on at home at this time?

709
00:27:53.850 --> 00:27:55.840
Like what's mom aware of?

710
00:27:55.840 --> 00:27:57.270
Oh, I kept it quiet from the parents.

711
00:27:57.270 --> 00:28:01.400
You know, like I led a double life really with my folks.

712
00:28:01.400 --> 00:28:03.980
And even with my wife and everything down through the years,

713
00:28:03.980 --> 00:28:05.810
I would do a lot of secret shit.

714
00:28:05.810 --> 00:28:07.543
You know, I would,

715
00:28:07.543 --> 00:28:09.110
I would stay over with friends, and you know,

716
00:28:09.110 --> 00:28:10.290
sometimes I would come home,

717
00:28:10.290 --> 00:28:12.320
and my poor mother would be like sitting in the kitchen

718
00:28:12.320 --> 00:28:14.650
at four o'clock in the morning waiting for me,

719
00:28:14.650 --> 00:28:17.720
and I'd walk in the door drunk, and you know,

720
00:28:17.720 --> 00:28:22.450
I felt bad about it, but I still felt like it was worth it

721
00:28:22.450 --> 00:28:23.550
at the time.

722
00:28:23.550 --> 00:28:24.660
Well, it's also that thing

723
00:28:24.660 --> 00:28:26.890
where you think you're getting away with this,

724
00:28:26.890 --> 00:28:28.880
that double life, that they're not aware

725
00:28:28.880 --> 00:28:32.020
of what you're doing, but it's pretty transparent.

726
00:28:32.020 --> 00:28:36.230
Yeah, yeah, yeah, it is what it is like.

727
00:28:36.230 --> 00:28:39.390
Yeah, I put my poor parents through a lot,

728
00:28:39.390 --> 00:28:42.110
you know, because later when I got into trouble,

729
00:28:42.110 --> 00:28:45.130
everybody around knows everybody and stuff like that.

730
00:28:45.130 --> 00:28:48.870
So when I got into trouble later, I got caught dealing.

731
00:28:48.870 --> 00:28:50.824
Everybody knew, you know?

732
00:28:50.824 --> 00:28:51.822
Right.

733
00:28:51.822 --> 00:28:52.827
I mean, how are they now?

734
00:28:52.827 --> 00:28:53.819
What do they think about this book

735
00:28:53.819 --> 00:28:55.099
and this potential TV show and all of that?

736
00:28:55.099 --> 00:28:57.118
It must be a mindblower.

737
00:28:57.118 --> 00:28:58.200
Well.

738
00:28:58.200 --> 00:28:59.868
Back, have you, you probably haven't been,

739
00:28:59.868 --> 00:29:01.171
have you been back home at all?

740
00:29:01.171 --> 00:29:02.390
Oh yeah, I've been home a lot of times.

741
00:29:02.390 --> 00:29:07.390
Yeah, I'm sure they don't like the stuff being brought up,

742
00:29:07.887 --> 00:29:09.150
but it is what it is.

743
00:29:09.150 --> 00:29:10.180
It's a positive story.

744
00:29:10.180 --> 00:29:11.700
I turn my life around.

745
00:29:11.700 --> 00:29:14.810
It's not like I'm still doing this kind of stuff, you know?

746
00:29:14.810 --> 00:29:15.950
Yeah, but just the idea

747
00:29:15.950 --> 00:29:17.790
that like there's a book out there,

748
00:29:17.790 --> 00:29:20.320
and you're kind of being feted, celebrated.

749
00:29:20.320 --> 00:29:23.600
Yeah, well, you know, my mother like said to me,

750
00:29:23.600 --> 00:29:24.433
she goes, Jesus Christ.

751
00:29:24.433 --> 00:29:25.890
You're not, you're not worried

752
00:29:25.890 --> 00:29:27.650
about people knowing what you did?

753
00:29:27.650 --> 00:29:29.480
And I'm like, if I gave a fuck,

754
00:29:29.480 --> 00:29:30.740
I wouldn't have wrote it in a book.

755
00:29:30.740 --> 00:29:33.215
Like, you know, I'm sorry you feel that way,

756
00:29:33.215 --> 00:29:35.900
but that's only natural I suppose.

757
00:29:35.900 --> 00:29:38.213
But that's that shame thing, right,

758
00:29:38.213 --> 00:29:40.320
that kind of emanates out of Catholicism.

759
00:29:40.320 --> 00:29:41.153
Yeah.

760
00:29:41.153 --> 00:29:43.810
Like we keep our, we keep our weaknesses private.

761
00:29:43.810 --> 00:29:47.400
Yeah, yeah, and you know, when I was a kid, I was like,

762
00:29:47.400 --> 00:29:49.070
I was super into the Catholicism.

763
00:29:49.070 --> 00:29:52.880
Like even though I didn't like being forced

764
00:29:52.880 --> 00:29:56.490
to go to church every week, I was an altar boy

765
00:29:56.490 --> 00:30:00.270
at the church, and that shit used to make me nervous

766
00:30:00.270 --> 00:30:01.830
as well because you gotta stand,

767
00:30:01.830 --> 00:30:04.550
sit up in front of everybody at the front of the church.

768
00:30:04.550 --> 00:30:06.950
And you know, if you're altar boy,

769
00:30:06.950 --> 00:30:09.220
you have to like ring the bell at certain times

770
00:30:09.220 --> 00:30:11.490
during the thing, and I would always be so nervous

771
00:30:11.490 --> 00:30:12.550
about that shit as well.

772
00:30:12.550 --> 00:30:14.950
I'd either miss the fucking time I was supposed to do it

773
00:30:14.950 --> 00:30:16.340
or ring it too early,

774
00:30:16.340 --> 00:30:19.510
or it was fucking mortifying, you know?

775
00:30:19.510 --> 00:30:21.110
Same shit with the water and the wine.

