about my embarrassing shit,

2284
01:30:21.750 --> 01:30:23.290
that scared the shit outta me.

2285
01:30:23.290 --> 01:30:25.420
So I was like intent

2286
01:30:25.420 --> 01:30:27.530
on not fucking telling anybody anything,

2287
01:30:27.530 --> 01:30:30.440
sit at the back, you know, keep to myself.

2288
01:30:30.440 --> 01:30:32.530
And so I sat down in the back,

2289
01:30:32.530 --> 01:30:36.938
and everybody was shaking my hand and saying hello.

2290
01:30:36.938 --> 01:30:39.040
And I was just trying to keep a low profile.

2291
01:30:39.040 --> 01:30:42.078
And at the start of the meeting, the guy says,

2292
01:30:42.078 --> 01:30:44.510
have we any newcomers here tonight?

2293
01:30:44.510 --> 01:30:47.350
And everybody like turns around, looks at me like,

2294
01:30:47.350 --> 01:30:51.220
and I would've like pretend fucking

2295
01:30:51.220 --> 01:30:53.860
or give a fake name or something like that and just leave.

2296
01:30:53.860 --> 01:30:56.570
But Bernard and Nile already knew who I was.

2297
01:30:56.570 --> 01:31:00.530
So they put up the hand, and I was like I'm Richie.

2298
01:31:00.530 --> 01:31:02.730
I'm an alcoholic and a drug addict.

2299
01:31:02.730 --> 01:31:04.530
And I had never, I don't think I had ever admitted that

2300
01:31:04.530 --> 01:31:05.370
before in a group.

2301
01:31:05.370 --> 01:31:07.700
Like, and I couldn't believe it.

2302
01:31:07.700 --> 01:31:09.750
They all fucking clapped.

2303
01:31:09.750 --> 01:31:13.680
And I was like, wow, do you people know who I am?

2304
01:31:13.680 --> 01:31:15.560
Like the things I have done.

2305
01:31:15.560 --> 01:31:16.810
And, but they didn't give a fuck.

2306
01:31:16.810 --> 01:31:20.180
Some of them did, but they didn't give a shit.

2307
01:31:20.180 --> 01:31:22.850
All they cared about was there's a dude here

2308
01:31:22.850 --> 01:31:25.910
who has a problem, and you know,

2309
01:31:25.910 --> 01:31:28.590
we're gonna help him out for fun and for free.

2310
01:31:28.590 --> 01:31:32.040
And it really, I couldn't believe they were clapping for me.

2311
01:31:32.040 --> 01:31:35.740
They're really like not what I was expecting, you know?

2312
01:31:35.740 --> 01:31:38.220
Yeah, so you say that out loud for the first time,

2313
01:31:38.220 --> 01:31:43.200
but at what point did you believe that about yourself?

2314
01:31:43.200 --> 01:31:44.193
Like prior to that

2315
01:31:44.193 --> 01:31:47.140
because you thought it was some other mental defect

2316
01:31:47.140 --> 01:31:50.370
or you were making rationalizations or excuses for yourself,

2317
01:31:50.370 --> 01:31:53.480
but deep down when your head hit the pillow, you knew,

2318
01:31:53.480 --> 01:31:56.699
like you knew you were an alcoholic and a drug addict.

2319
01:31:56.699 --> 01:31:58.690
When I started drinking at the age of 15 or 16,

2320
01:31:58.690 --> 01:32:01.980
I knew I had a problem back then, but.

2321
01:32:01.980 --> 01:32:03.120
You push it way down.

2322
01:32:03.120 --> 01:32:05.860
Yeah, like I remember one time going to the doctor.

2323
01:32:05.860 --> 01:32:07.540
You know, when you go to the doctor's office,

2324
01:32:07.540 --> 01:32:09.670
and there's a bunch of leaflets and shit like that

2325
01:32:09.670 --> 01:32:12.290
sitting around, and it's in Ireland, same as here.

2326
01:32:12.290 --> 01:32:13.550
You'd have a bunch of leaflets and shit

2327
01:32:13.550 --> 01:32:15.120
in the doctor's office.

2328
01:32:15.120 --> 01:32:17.335
I remember when I was a kid, like a teenager,

2329
01:32:17.335 --> 01:32:19.390
I saw one of these leaflets,

2330
01:32:19.390 --> 01:32:22.170
and it was an alcoholic questionnaire.

2331
01:32:22.170 --> 01:32:24.413
I think it's called "The 20 Questions."

2332
01:32:24.413 --> 01:32:25.619
Yeah, yeah.

2333
01:32:25.619 --> 01:32:26.954
I think that's what it's called.

2334
01:32:26.954 --> 01:32:28.480
So I remember as a kid fucking opening this shit up

2335
01:32:28.480 --> 01:32:29.850
when I was at the doctor's office,

2336
01:32:29.850 --> 01:32:32.500
and I had just discovered drinking at this time,

2337
01:32:32.500 --> 01:32:34.430
and I'm reading through the questions.

2338
01:32:34.430 --> 01:32:37.030
Do you ever do things you regret while you're drinking?

2339
01:32:37.030 --> 01:32:38.350
Ah, who doesn't.

2340
01:32:38.350 --> 01:32:40.250
Do you ever lie about your drinking?

2341
01:32:40.250 --> 01:32:41.410
Of course.

2342
01:32:41.410 --> 01:32:43.539
You know, have you ever blacked out?

2343
01:32:43.539 --> 01:32:45.280
Ah, it happens to everybody.

2344
01:32:45.280 --> 01:32:48.694
And I remember back then, when I had done the questionnaire,

2345
01:32:48.694 --> 01:32:52.752
I probably got 16 or 17 out of 20.

2346
01:32:52.752 --> 01:32:56.800
And if you ever do that questionnaire, they say one yes

2347
01:32:56.800 --> 01:32:58.710
means you might be an alcoholic.

2348
01:32:58.710 --> 01:33:01.280
Two yeses mean you're probably an alcoholic.

2349
01:33:01.280 --> 01:33:04.420
Three or more, you are definitely an alcoholic.

2350
01:33:04.420 --> 01:33:06.530
So I saw it in black and white

2351
01:33:06.530 --> 01:33:08.650
when I was a fucking teenager,

2352
01:33:08.650 --> 01:33:10.970
but I thought it was a joke.

2353
01:33:10.970 --> 01:33:13.140
You know, I was like, everybody drinks in Ireland, you know.

2354
01:33:13.140 --> 01:33:14.760
It's like, it's in our culture.

2355
01:33:14.760 --> 01:33:15.680
It's in our blood.

2356
01:33:15.680 --> 01:33:19.421
Like, you know, so I knew I had a problem from the start,

2357
01:33:19.421 --> 01:33:22.255
but when you're doing the steps, right,

2358
01:33:22.255 --> 01:33:26.270
it's admit it, you're powerless over drugs and alcohol,

2359
01:33:26.270 --> 01:33:28.130
and your life is unmanageable.

2360
01:33:28.130 --> 01:33:30.946
So I knew I was powerless from a teenager,

2361
01:33:30.946 --> 01:33:33.924
but I thought my life was manageable.

2362
01:33:33.924 --> 01:33:37.820
If you looked from the outside looking in,

2363
01:33:37.820 --> 01:33:41.280
you'd say this guy's a fucking, a fiend, like, you know,

2364
01:33:41.280 --> 01:33:45.630
but until the very end, I probably hadn't admitted

2365
01:33:45.630 --> 01:33:48.140
that second part that my life was unmanageable.

2366
01:33:48.140 --> 01:33:49.481
Right, right.

2367
01:33:49.481 --> 01:33:50.540
And that's the baffling thing.

2368
01:33:50.540 --> 01:33:53.390
Cause any outside observer would say

2369
01:33:53.390 --> 01:33:55.710
this is nothing but chaos and insanity,

2370
01:33:55.710 --> 01:34:00.180
but your lived experience was, right, this is under control.

2371
01:34:00.180 --> 01:34:01.640
I'm managing this all right.

2372
01:34:01.640 --> 01:34:04.121
Yeah, in my own head, you know,

2373
01:34:04.121 --> 01:34:08.180
but obviously not in everybody else's head.

2374
01:34:08.180 --> 01:34:09.013
No.

2375
01:34:09.013 --> 01:34:11.320
The people I was working with, you know,

2376
01:34:11.320 --> 01:34:15.052
the dolls I was seeing, my wife, obviously.

2377
01:34:15.052 --> 01:34:16.650
Yeah, we're gonna get to the wife.

2378
01:34:16.650 --> 01:34:20.150
But first, you know, one of the things I appreciated

2379
01:34:20.150 --> 01:34:22.250
about the book is your candor

2380
01:34:22.250 --> 01:34:24.930
around the character defect piece.

2381
01:34:24.930 --> 01:34:27.500
Because there is this idea that when you get sober

2382
01:34:27.500 --> 01:34:30.000
like it's just about getting rid of the drugs and alcohol,

2383
01:34:30.000 --> 01:34:32.450
and then all my problems are gonna go away.

2384
01:34:32.450 --> 01:34:35.670
And what you don't realize is that then, you know,

2385
01:34:35.670 --> 01:34:38.640
you have all of these emotions that come to the surface

2386
01:34:38.640 --> 01:34:40.140
that become very unmanageable

2387
01:34:40.140 --> 01:34:41.730
until you learn these new tools

2388
01:34:41.730 --> 01:34:43.940
for how to work through them.

2389
01:34:43.940 --> 01:34:48.940
And in your case, like a lot of it goes back to the anger.

2390
01:34:49.170 --> 01:34:54.170
Yeah, like basically when you're getting sober, right,

2391
01:34:55.870 --> 01:34:58.750
it's really difficult when they take away your medicine

2392
01:34:58.750 --> 01:35:00.460
because the booze is your medicine.

2393
01:35:00.460 --> 01:35:02.480
If you're an alcoholic, the booze is what you use

2394
01:35:02.480 --> 01:35:05.410
to feel good or to deal with all your problems.

2395
01:35:05.410 --> 01:35:07.895
For me, like any time I had any kind of a feeling,

2396
01:35:07.895 --> 01:35:11.170
the impulse was to drink or get high.

2397
01:35:11.170 --> 01:35:13.050
Like if I was happy about something,

2398
01:35:13.050 --> 01:35:14.330
yay, let's celebrate.

2399
01:35:14.330 --> 01:35:16.820
If you're sad about something, drown your sorrows.

2400
01:35:16.820 --> 01:35:18.460
If you're angry about something,

2401
01:35:18.460 --> 01:35:20.100
need a drink to calm you down.

2402
01:35:20.100 --> 01:35:24.730
It was literally my solution for everything, even boredom.

2403
01:35:24.730 --> 01:35:25.950
Fuck, I have nothing to do.

2404
01:35:25.950 --> 01:35:27.590
Let's go to the bar.

2405
01:35:27.590 --> 01:35:31.100
So if you have a problem with drinking and drugs,

2406
01:35:31.100 --> 01:35:32.520
like that's your life.

2407
01:35:32.520 --> 01:35:37.400
And then to suddenly have your comfort taken away,

2408
01:35:37.400 --> 01:35:40.370
you're raw as fuck, like, you know,

2409
01:35:40.370 --> 01:35:44.400
so when someone's newly sober,

2410
01:35:44.400 --> 01:35:46.350
they're definitely really irritable.

2411
01:35:46.350 --> 01:35:50.730
And like you were saying with the defects of character,

2412
01:35:50.730 --> 01:35:52.730
there's no such thing as a perfect person.

2413
01:35:52.730 --> 01:35:54.930
I still have defects of character obviously,

2414
01:35:56.739 --> 01:36:00.140
but they're more obvious when the booze is gone,

2415
01:36:00.140 --> 01:36:01.440
and your head is clear,

2416
01:36:01.440 --> 01:36:06.300
and you have to get real about what these problems you have.

2417
01:36:06.300 --> 01:36:11.300
Like for me, I would say, yeah, quick to anger was one.

2418
01:36:12.830 --> 01:36:17.830
You know, I probably got as many beatings as I gave,

2419
01:36:18.600 --> 01:36:22.473
you know, but violence was a way to solve problems.

2420
01:36:26.960 --> 01:36:29.250
I never hit my misses or my kids or anything like that.

2421
01:36:29.250 --> 01:36:31.860
But other dudes, like, you know,

2422
01:36:31.860 --> 01:36:34.900
and that's not how you behave.

2423
01:36:34.900 --> 01:36:38.450
Like when I came to the meetings, they says,

2424
01:36:38.450 --> 01:36:39.943
it's a spiritual program.

2425
01:36:40.790 --> 01:36:44.290
And I said, what the fuck is spiritual?

2426
01:36:44.290 --> 01:36:45.851
And I have a college education,

2427
01:36:45.851 --> 01:36:49.290
but I never used the word spiritual.

2428
01:36:49.290 --> 01:36:51.810
It wasn't in my vocabulary like, and I was like,

2429
01:36:51.810 --> 01:36:52.990
what does that mean?

2430
01:36:52.990 --> 01:36:55.210
Do we all fucking sit around and do yoga

2431
01:36:55.210 --> 01:36:57.040
or become vegan?

2432
01:36:57.040 --> 01:36:58.732
Or what the fuck is that?

2433
01:36:58.732 --> 01:37:01.140
You know, that's what I was,

2434
01:37:01.140 --> 01:37:02.340
that's what I thought originally.

2435
01:37:02.340 --> 01:37:03.794
Maybe! (Rich laughing)

2436
01:37:03.794 --> 01:37:08.794
Not me, but I, but yeah, so I heard

2437
01:37:08.920 --> 01:37:11.070
like you'd hear these people at the meetings

2438
01:37:11.070 --> 01:37:13.653
and they're like, yeah, it's a spiritual program.

2439
01:37:14.532 --> 01:37:16.440
I said what the fuck is spiritual?

2440
01:37:16.440 --> 01:37:18.950
And the best definition I got,

2441
01:37:18.950 --> 01:37:22.440
an old priest I talked to at one of the meetings, he said,

2442
01:37:22.440 --> 01:37:25.853
spirituality is freedom from the bondage of self.

2443
01:37:26.690 --> 01:37:29.170
So I had bondage of self

2444
01:37:29.170 --> 01:37:31.570
that's why I was drinking and doing all these drugs.

2445
01:37:31.570 --> 01:37:34.230
I was like, okay, that sounds cool.

2446
01:37:34.230 --> 01:37:37.730
The booze and the coke used to be my spirituality.

2447
01:37:37.730 --> 01:37:39.031
How the fuck do I,

2448
01:37:39.031 --> 01:37:43.050
how do I feel good now without that stuff?

2449
01:37:43.050 --> 01:37:45.294
And they said, it's very simple.

2450
01:37:45.294 --> 01:37:49.650
You just, you just do whatever your sponsor suggests.

2451
01:37:49.650 --> 01:37:52.010
You try to be honest.

2452
01:37:52.010 --> 01:37:53.430
You try to help other people

2453
01:37:53.430 --> 01:37:56.220
instead of just thinking about yourself,

2454
01:37:56.220 --> 01:37:59.920
and you do other shit like praying and meditating

2455
01:37:59.920 --> 01:38:01.380
if you wanna do that kind of stuff.

2456
01:38:01.380 --> 01:38:04.463
Like I didn't do that kind of stuff at the beginning, but,

2457
01:38:06.950 --> 01:38:11.309
yeah, I slowly learned the tools to not have to drink

2458
01:38:11.309 --> 01:38:14.640
and get high anymore.

2459
01:38:14.640 --> 01:38:18.040
And it was a learning process.

2460
01:38:18.040 --> 01:38:22.170
And slowly my feelings started to become more normal.

2461
01:38:22.170 --> 01:38:23.490
The highs weren't so high.

2462
01:38:23.490 --> 01:38:26.754
The lows weren't so low, you know?

2463
01:38:26.754 --> 01:38:30.051
Right, and there's that fear that comes with that

2464
01:38:30.051 --> 01:38:33.610
because there is an addiction to those highs and lows

2465
01:38:33.610 --> 01:38:34.443
on some level.

2466
01:38:34.443 --> 01:38:36.570
Like what is my life gonna be like,

2467
01:38:36.570 --> 01:38:39.447
if I'm just flat lining all the time?

2468
01:38:39.447 --> 01:38:41.890
You know, I can't live that way.

2469
01:38:41.890 --> 01:38:42.723
Yeah.

2470
01:38:42.723 --> 01:38:43.751
It's gonna be boring.

2471
01:38:43.751 --> 01:38:45.020
It's gonna be intolerable.

2472
01:38:45.020 --> 01:38:49.470
Yeah, I thought, before I actually decided to get sober.

2473
01:38:49.470 --> 01:38:52.040
Like when I decided to get sober, there was no more options.

2474
01:38:52.040 --> 01:38:54.650
I was like it's either do this or die.

2475
01:38:54.650 --> 01:38:57.890
But before that, the concept of like getting sober,

2476
01:38:57.890 --> 01:38:59.740
maybe even going to meetings or something like that,

2477
01:38:59.740 --> 01:39:02.460
I thought it would be like the most boring shit ever.

2478
01:39:02.460 --> 01:39:03.940
I thought it would be like a bunch of people

2479
01:39:03.940 --> 01:39:07.670
fucking hanging out in the room, trying not to drink,

2480
01:39:07.670 --> 01:39:09.720
you know, like kinda sad and pathetic,

2481
01:39:09.720 --> 01:39:13.089
but it turned out to be the exact opposite for me.

2482
01:39:13.089 --> 01:39:16.250
The people I've met in recovery

2483
01:39:16.250 --> 01:39:18.410
are the most interesting people.

2484
01:39:18.410 --> 01:39:21.140
The people who were like me so fucked up

2485
01:39:21.140 --> 01:39:23.770
that they couldn't do it anymore.

2486
01:39:23.770 --> 01:39:24.603
You know?

2487
01:39:24.603 --> 01:39:26.730
And there was a lot of fun around that.

2488
01:39:26.730 --> 01:39:30.860
And I learned how to do normal things sober.

2489
01:39:30.860 --> 01:39:34.130
Like there's this thing that they do,

2490
01:39:34.130 --> 01:39:38.060
another new word for me was fellowship.

2491
01:39:38.060 --> 01:39:40.763
So I'm like what the fuck is fellowship?

2492
01:39:42.730 --> 01:39:45.640
Bernard said to me one day when I was new at the meetings,

2493
01:39:45.640 --> 01:39:47.503
I was just, I was just getting like,

2494
01:39:47.503 --> 01:39:49.290
I was just getting stuck in at the start.

2495
01:39:49.290 --> 01:39:51.610
And he says, we're going to meet for coffee.

2496
01:39:51.610 --> 01:39:53.220
Meet me at the coffee shop.

2497
01:39:53.220 --> 01:39:54.653
I says, go for coffee?

2498
01:39:55.651 --> 01:39:57.420
What the fuck are we gonna do there?

2499
01:39:57.420 --> 01:40:01.123
And he goes, we're gonna talk and drink coffee.

2500
01:40:02.071 --> 01:40:06.600
And that was like, that was weird to me as well

2501
01:40:06.600 --> 01:40:07.930
cause since I was a kid,

2502
01:40:07.930 --> 01:40:10.314
when you're in a social fucking surrounding,

2503
01:40:10.314 --> 01:40:12.050
you wanna have a beer.

2504
01:40:12.050 --> 01:40:14.740
And, but it was a catch 22 with me,

2505
01:40:14.740 --> 01:40:16.600
like before I got sober,

2506
01:40:16.600 --> 01:40:19.080
if I was in a social setting, some shit like this,

2507
01:40:19.080 --> 01:40:20.700
where I didn't really know the people,

2508
01:40:20.700 --> 01:40:24.572
and I might feel nervous, I'd want a beer just to feel okay.

2509
01:40:24.572 --> 01:40:27.380
And then the problem was once I started drinking the beer,

2510
01:40:27.380 --> 01:40:28.840
I drank too much beer.

2511
01:40:28.840 --> 01:40:30.467
And then I started making a fool of myself.

2512
01:40:30.467 --> 01:40:32.570
So it was even when I was drinking,

2513
01:40:32.570 --> 01:40:34.490
it was a no win situation.

2514
01:40:34.490 --> 01:40:37.330
So we had to like, so I remember the first time

2515
01:40:37.330 --> 01:40:39.410
we went to the coffee shop, and we were drinking coffee

2516
01:40:39.410 --> 01:40:40.913
and just chatting.

2517
01:40:40.913 --> 01:40:42.230
It was like, it was weird like,

2518
01:40:42.230 --> 01:40:44.600
but I got used to it fairly quick

2519
01:40:44.600 --> 01:40:48.890
because there was something about being around other people

2520
01:40:48.890 --> 01:40:52.230
who were the same as me, who had the same problem as me.

2521
01:40:52.230 --> 01:40:54.430
I found it to have a connection

2522
01:40:54.430 --> 01:40:56.970
to other people who have my problem.

2523
01:40:56.970 --> 01:40:59.970
There's something about talking to another fucking drunk

2524
01:40:59.970 --> 01:41:04.670
or another addict that they understand you, you know?

2525
01:41:04.670 --> 01:41:09.250
So, and I used to trip out so much about it at the start.

2526
01:41:09.250 --> 01:41:12.283
I'm like, oh, how am I never gonna drink again fucking?

2527
01:41:12.283 --> 01:41:14.170
What if my parents die?

2528
01:41:14.170 --> 01:41:17.230
Or what if my daughter gets married in 20 years,

2529
01:41:17.230 --> 01:41:18.063
and I'm at her wedding,

2530
01:41:18.063 --> 01:41:21.140
will I not be able to have a glass of champagne or whatever?

2531
01:41:21.140 --> 01:41:24.500
And Bernard, he says to me, he says, nevermind that shit.

2532
01:41:24.500 --> 01:41:27.120
He says, we do it one day at a time.

2533
01:41:27.120 --> 01:41:28.970
So today you don't feel like drinking.

2534
01:41:28.970 --> 01:41:30.320
Maybe tomorrow you won't either.

2535
01:41:30.320 --> 01:41:33.520
Don't worry about fucking 20 years time, you know?

