I get 'em every month, yeah.

2743
01:50:26.970 --> 01:50:29.397
So how does the book come about,

2744
01:50:29.397 --> 01:50:32.373
and this relationship with John and Dave?

2745
01:50:33.999 --> 01:50:35.330
Oh, so.

2746
01:50:35.330 --> 01:50:38.300
I mean the book opens with them talking about

2747
01:50:38.300 --> 01:50:42.830
how they met you and kind of it being its own little miracle

2748
01:50:42.830 --> 01:50:44.460
because ordinarily they would've never,

2749
01:50:44.460 --> 01:50:46.430
you just sort of cold emailed them.

2750
01:50:46.430 --> 01:50:47.760
Yeah, I did.

2751
01:50:47.760 --> 01:50:49.520
Ordinarily they would've never even opened that email.

2752
01:50:49.520 --> 01:50:51.210
They didn't know me from Adam.

2753
01:50:51.210 --> 01:50:52.380
So, so basically.

2754
01:50:52.380 --> 01:50:53.870
And explain who these guys are.

2755
01:50:53.870 --> 01:50:57.323
Okay, so John Altschuler and David Krinsky,

2756
01:50:57.323 --> 01:51:00.041
they're the co-creators of "Silicon Valley,"

2757
01:51:00.041 --> 01:51:02.170
and they were show runners on "King of the Hill."

2758
01:51:02.170 --> 01:51:05.706
They wrote "Blades of Glory," starring Will Ferrell.

2759
01:51:05.706 --> 01:51:10.706
Yeah, they're successful writers and show runners.

2760
01:51:12.480 --> 01:51:13.540
Yeah, they're big time Hollywood show runners and writers.

2761
01:51:13.540 --> 01:51:17.343
Yeah, and the way it came about, it was a funny thing.

2762
01:51:19.040 --> 01:51:23.240
So one of my buddies, a guy called Sean, Sean Mann.

2763
01:51:23.240 --> 01:51:24.790
He's another actor.

2764
01:51:24.790 --> 01:51:26.500
We moved to LA around the same time.

2765
01:51:26.500 --> 01:51:27.930
He's a really good guy.

2766
01:51:27.930 --> 01:51:31.260
And he was working on this comedy project,

2767
01:51:31.260 --> 01:51:34.060
and I was helping him do a little bit of producing on it.

2768
01:51:34.060 --> 01:51:37.510
And if you guys wanna see it, I think it's on YouTube.

2769
01:51:37.510 --> 01:51:38.343
It's pretty funny.

2770
01:51:38.343 --> 01:51:40.210
He did like a proof of concept.

2771
01:51:40.210 --> 01:51:42.160
It's called "Roommates."

2772
01:51:42.160 --> 01:51:45.580
So he says, see if you can get me someone big

2773
01:51:45.580 --> 01:51:48.870
attached to this, and if you can help me out.

2774
01:51:48.870 --> 01:51:50.210
So I was just helping Sean out.

2775
01:51:50.210 --> 01:51:53.030
So I was like, this is a good comedy.

2776
01:51:53.030 --> 01:51:56.400
It's kind of an out there comedy that he was,

2777
01:51:56.400 --> 01:51:58.160
he had created.

2778
01:51:58.160 --> 01:52:00.440
And so I looked at who were the best comedy people.

2779
01:52:00.440 --> 01:52:03.730
And at the time "Silicon Valley" was one of the top ones.

2780
01:52:03.730 --> 01:52:07.270
So I reached out to like a couple of people.

2781
01:52:07.270 --> 01:52:09.350
The first one was Danny McBride.

2782
01:52:09.350 --> 01:52:11.530
I got Danny McBride's email,

2783
01:52:11.530 --> 01:52:15.430
and I emailed him, and then his assistant got back and said,

2784
01:52:15.430 --> 01:52:17.710
we don't accept unsolicited materials.

2785
01:52:17.710 --> 01:52:19.882
And then I sent it to John,

2786
01:52:19.882 --> 01:52:24.710
and John responded, and he said this is cool.

2787
01:52:24.710 --> 01:52:27.697
Let's meet, and we met up with John, and.

2788
01:52:27.697 --> 01:52:30.340
Right, which is highly, highly unusual.

2789
01:52:30.340 --> 01:52:31.698
Yeah, that.

2790
01:52:31.698 --> 01:52:33.190
That's not, you know, that's not how things work.

2791
01:52:33.190 --> 01:52:35.540
That kind of shit doesn't happen really.

2792
01:52:35.540 --> 01:52:37.955
Yeah, usually if you send unsolicited materials

2793
01:52:37.955 --> 01:52:39.190
to top people.

2794
01:52:39.190 --> 01:52:41.290
For legal reasons alone, they don't do it.

2795
01:52:41.290 --> 01:52:42.750
Other than like who is this guy?

2796
01:52:42.750 --> 01:52:45.010
Like you're not gonna get the time of day from anybody.

2797
01:52:45.010 --> 01:52:46.110
Yeah, exactly.

2798
01:52:46.110 --> 01:52:49.270
But it just turns out that they were really nice guys,

2799
01:52:49.270 --> 01:52:51.340
and we ended up meeting up with them,

2800
01:52:51.340 --> 01:52:54.140
and that particular project wasn't a fit for John,

2801
01:52:54.140 --> 01:52:57.230
but he said, I like you guys, keep sending me stuff.

2802
01:52:57.230 --> 01:52:58.870
So I sent him another couple of things,

2803
01:52:58.870 --> 01:53:00.060
and he passed on those.

2804
01:53:00.060 --> 01:53:03.790
And then I had written my original draft of the book,

2805
01:53:03.790 --> 01:53:06.060
and I sent that to him, and he liked it.

2806
01:53:06.060 --> 01:53:08.750
And then he read like 50 pages of it.

2807
01:53:08.750 --> 01:53:10.040
And he says, I like this,

2808
01:53:10.040 --> 01:53:11.980
but I don't really know where it's going.

2809
01:53:11.980 --> 01:53:16.230
So then I told him about my past, and he was like,

2810
01:53:16.230 --> 01:53:17.470
let's meet again.

2811
01:53:17.470 --> 01:53:19.530
Cause the first time that we met, he had no idea

2812
01:53:19.530 --> 01:53:21.300
I used to be a gangster or anything like that.

2813
01:53:21.300 --> 01:53:22.540
I'm not scary in person.

2814
01:53:22.540 --> 01:53:23.740
I'm friendly like,

2815
01:53:23.740 --> 01:53:27.272
and then we met up again, and I told him a couple of yarns,

2816
01:53:27.272 --> 01:53:29.880
and he's like, wow, this is crazy.

2817
01:53:29.880 --> 01:53:31.370
Do you wanna partner on it?

2818
01:53:31.370 --> 01:53:32.900
And I said, okay.

2819
01:53:32.900 --> 01:53:37.900
And then, so first of all, he has another show coming out.

2820
01:53:38.220 --> 01:53:40.070
I'm not allowed to say what it is,

2821
01:53:40.070 --> 01:53:42.890
but basically it's about somebody who's an author.

2822
01:53:42.890 --> 01:53:46.620
And then he put us in touch with our book agents,

2823
01:53:46.620 --> 01:53:49.673
and the book agents read the book, and they were like

2824
01:53:49.673 --> 01:53:53.030
wow, this is pretty crazy, but I don't know how to sell it.

2825
01:53:53.030 --> 01:53:55.330
And then John had the idea of rewriting the book

2826
01:53:55.330 --> 01:53:57.499
in the format of the 12 steps

2827
01:53:57.499 --> 01:54:00.350
cause so it would be shorter and more accessible

2828
01:54:00.350 --> 01:54:01.890
to what my story really is.

2829
01:54:01.890 --> 01:54:04.410
And then we rewrote the book together,

2830
01:54:04.410 --> 01:54:08.350
and the book is coming out on May 24th,

2831
01:54:08.350 --> 01:54:12.440
and it's gonna be a TV show as well.

2832
01:54:12.440 --> 01:54:14.380
So what's the deal with the TV show?

2833
01:54:14.380 --> 01:54:17.600
Like is that a pilot deal or a series deal?

2834
01:54:17.600 --> 01:54:19.730
What's the status of development there?

2835
01:54:19.730 --> 01:54:21.930
Like how, you know, cause it's one thing like,

2836
01:54:21.930 --> 01:54:23.280
oh, there's gonna be a show.

2837
01:54:23.280 --> 01:54:25.500
There's a long, you know, a lot of things have to happen

2838
01:54:25.500 --> 01:54:28.000
before something ends up on the air, right?

2839
01:54:28.000 --> 01:54:31.640
Well, we took it into John's manager

2840
01:54:31.640 --> 01:54:34.703
before the book was done, and he said,

2841
01:54:34.703 --> 01:54:38.470
you should get a book deal first

2842
01:54:38.470 --> 01:54:40.139
cause it's easier to green light.

2843
01:54:40.139 --> 01:54:42.360
And then we got the book deal,

2844
01:54:42.360 --> 01:54:44.070
and we have a bunch of people

2845
01:54:44.070 --> 01:54:45.877
who are interested in it right now.

2846
01:54:45.877 --> 01:54:48.430
We dunno where it's gonna land yet.

2847
01:54:48.430 --> 01:54:49.263
Yeah.

2848
01:54:50.237 --> 01:54:52.240
But I can't really say who's looking at it,

2849
01:54:52.240 --> 01:54:53.400
but some cool people.

2850
01:54:53.400 --> 01:54:54.610
It's exciting, man.

2851
01:54:54.610 --> 01:54:55.443
Yeah.

2852
01:54:55.443 --> 01:54:56.610
It's quite an arc.

2853
01:54:56.610 --> 01:54:58.097
It's crazy.

2854
01:54:58.097 --> 01:54:59.620
When you look back on the whole thing,

2855
01:54:59.620 --> 01:55:01.139
it's pretty miraculous.

2856
01:55:01.139 --> 01:55:03.478
Yeah, it's kind of unbelievable.

2857
01:55:03.478 --> 01:55:08.478
Like number one that I'm alive after all this kinda stuff,

2858
01:55:08.710 --> 01:55:12.940
and yeah, it's pretty crazy.

2859
01:55:12.940 --> 01:55:15.830
Do you find that that makes it easier

2860
01:55:15.830 --> 01:55:20.818
to connect with gratitude and all of that?

2861
01:55:20.818 --> 01:55:21.822
Yeah, absolutely.

2862
01:55:21.822 --> 01:55:25.860
Like, you know, they told me when I got sober,

2863
01:55:25.860 --> 01:55:28.020
if you stay grateful, you won't ever drink again.

2864
01:55:28.020 --> 01:55:30.560
So I have a lot of things to be grateful for.

2865
01:55:30.560 --> 01:55:35.560
And, yeah.

2866
01:55:36.020 --> 01:55:38.293
I have a crazy life today.

2867
01:55:39.600 --> 01:55:42.480
But it's pretty balanced now.

2868
01:55:42.480 --> 01:55:47.090
Yeah, yeah, the only drama I have is on the stage now.

2869
01:55:47.090 --> 01:55:49.410
Thank God, and try and keep it that way.

2870
01:55:49.410 --> 01:55:51.820
And meanwhile, you're still auditioning

2871
01:55:51.820 --> 01:55:53.920
and doing that whole, doing that whole deal.

2872
01:55:53.920 --> 01:55:56.510
You did some movie with Halle Berry, right?

2873
01:55:56.510 --> 01:55:59.159
Yeah, I did that a few years ago.

2874
01:55:59.159 --> 01:56:00.440
That was called "Kings,"

2875
01:56:00.440 --> 01:56:02.238
and last year I was.

2876
01:56:02.238 --> 01:56:03.071
I didn't see that one.

2877
01:56:03.071 --> 01:56:05.010
Yeah, that was about the Rodney King riots.

2878
01:56:05.010 --> 01:56:08.030
And I did, last year I did "Days of Our Lives,"

2879
01:56:08.030 --> 01:56:11.217
and "NCIS," and I've done "Blue Bloods,"

2880
01:56:11.217 --> 01:56:12.790
"Criminal Minds."

2881
01:56:12.790 --> 01:56:13.623
All the procedurals.

2882
01:56:13.623 --> 01:56:16.670
"MacGyver," all that kind of stuff.

2883
01:56:16.670 --> 01:56:20.670
I've been bad guy of the week a lot of times, yeah.

2884
01:56:20.670 --> 01:56:22.380
That's cool, man.

2885
01:56:22.380 --> 01:56:27.380
Well, let's round this out with some words of wisdom

2886
01:56:28.976 --> 01:56:33.939
for the person out there who's still suffering,

2887
01:56:33.939 --> 01:56:37.660
whether or not they're an alcoholic or a drug addict

2888
01:56:37.660 --> 01:56:41.900
or just battling with some kind of substance

2889
01:56:41.900 --> 01:56:45.300
or addiction related issue.

2890
01:56:45.300 --> 01:56:49.010
How do you communicate to that person?

2891
01:56:49.010 --> 01:56:52.050
Throw them a lifeline and kind of, you know,

2892
01:56:52.050 --> 01:56:56.040
help them figure out a better path forward.

2893
01:56:56.040 --> 01:56:57.960
Well, I would just say like,

2894
01:56:57.960 --> 01:57:02.160
no matter how bad you think things are, it can still,

2895
01:57:02.160 --> 01:57:05.240
you can still have, it can still be fixed.

2896
01:57:05.240 --> 01:57:06.610
Like I kind of thought

2897
01:57:06.610 --> 01:57:10.750
that I was just gonna be messed up forever

2898
01:57:10.750 --> 01:57:13.918
and that I didn't think that it would work for me.

2899
01:57:13.918 --> 01:57:18.500
And I've seen it working for a lot of people.

2900
01:57:18.500 --> 01:57:22.192
So all you have to do is ask for help,

2901
01:57:22.192 --> 01:57:23.400
and the help is there if you wanna take it.

2902
01:57:23.400 --> 01:57:25.470
Easier said than done sometimes.

2903
01:57:25.470 --> 01:57:27.570
Yeah, you have to be fully cooked.

2904
01:57:27.570 --> 01:57:29.934
You know, the best advice I ever got

2905
01:57:29.934 --> 01:57:33.337
when I was out and about,

2906
01:57:33.337 --> 01:57:36.633
one of those sober guys, I was working with him,

2907
01:57:36.633 --> 01:57:41.633
and I came in really hung over like, and he says,

2908
01:57:41.830 --> 01:57:45.223
why do you do this to yourself?

2909
01:57:46.461 --> 01:57:48.050
And I looked at him, and I was like,

2910
01:57:48.050 --> 01:57:49.400
you think I'm an alcoholic?

2911
01:57:50.610 --> 01:57:52.910
He says, of course you're a fucking alcoholic.

2912
01:57:54.216 --> 01:57:56.320
And I was like why?

2913
01:57:56.320 --> 01:57:59.510
He's like, you're fucking, you're doing Coke with hookers

2914
01:57:59.510 --> 01:58:00.343
in motels.

2915
01:58:00.343 --> 01:58:03.240
Like fucking non-alcoholic don't do that shit.

2916
01:58:03.240 --> 01:58:06.558
And then I was like,

2917
01:58:06.558 --> 01:58:08.150
well, do you think I should go to the meetings?

2918
01:58:08.150 --> 01:58:09.650
He goes, no, not yet.

2919
01:58:09.650 --> 01:58:13.200
He says, keep on doing it until you can't do it anymore.

2920
01:58:13.200 --> 01:58:15.130
If you're not ready, it won't work.

2921
01:58:15.130 --> 01:58:16.510
He said, you have to.

2922
01:58:16.510 --> 01:58:17.343
Research.

2923
01:58:17.343 --> 01:58:21.050
Yeah, he says, keep going until you're cooked.

2924
01:58:21.050 --> 01:58:22.870
And then you'll know when you can't do it anymore,

2925
01:58:22.870 --> 01:58:23.713
then you go.

2926
01:58:24.860 --> 01:58:27.530
Yeah, if you're ready, you're ready.

2927
01:58:27.530 --> 01:58:29.260
It's all about willingness.

2928
01:58:29.260 --> 01:58:31.513
Yeah.

2929
01:58:31.513 --> 01:58:34.220
If you can summon that willingness and do the thing.

2930
01:58:34.220 --> 01:58:38.810
Like yourself, I've seen so many lives

2931
01:58:38.810 --> 01:58:40.940
changed and transformed, so it is possible.

2932
01:58:40.940 --> 01:58:45.577
And I think the real inspirational piece in your story

2933
01:58:45.577 --> 01:58:47.520
relates to that arc.

2934
01:58:47.520 --> 01:58:50.380
Like, honestly, your story's so insane.

2935
01:58:50.380 --> 01:58:53.130
So if you could figure this out and get sober,

2936
01:58:53.130 --> 01:58:57.102
like I think it provides a lot of hope to a lot of people.

2937
01:58:57.102 --> 01:58:57.970
Well, I didn't figure it out on my own either.

2938
01:58:57.970 --> 01:59:00.950
Like really, I owe my life to that guy Bernard

2939
01:59:00.950 --> 01:59:03.794
who brought me to my meeting, to the meetings.

2940
01:59:03.794 --> 01:59:04.880
Who you, the book is dedicated to him.

2941
01:59:04.880 --> 01:59:06.110
Yeah, he saved my life.

2942
01:59:06.110 --> 01:59:08.915
Like I wouldn't be alive if it weren't for that man.

2943
01:59:08.915 --> 01:59:10.056
How's he doing now?

2944
01:59:10.056 --> 01:59:11.196
He's good.

2945
01:59:11.196 --> 01:59:12.029
He's over in Canada, and he's married,

2946
01:59:12.029 --> 01:59:12.880
and he has a little baby.

2947
01:59:12.880 --> 01:59:14.730
Is he still your sponsor?

2948
01:59:14.730 --> 01:59:17.830
No, no, I have a new one now, but yeah,

2949
01:59:17.830 --> 01:59:20.170
cause when he moved home, I got a local guy,

2950
01:59:20.170 --> 01:59:25.110
but no, we still keep in touch, and yeah, I owe him a lot.

2951
01:59:25.110 --> 01:59:26.736
Yeah, good, man.

2952
01:59:26.736 --> 01:59:28.040
Well, I'm super proud of you.

2953
01:59:28.040 --> 01:59:30.250
I've had the privilege of bearing witness

2954
01:59:30.250 --> 01:59:32.630
to part of this arc.

2955
01:59:32.630 --> 01:59:34.290
I remember when you were telling stories

2956
01:59:34.290 --> 01:59:37.659
about San Francisco, like way back in the day,

2957
01:59:37.659 --> 01:59:39.412
and you've come a long way, my friend.

2958
01:59:39.412 --> 01:59:41.450
So I'm excited for this book to come out,

2959
01:59:41.450 --> 01:59:44.969
and for everybody to, you know, get a taste

2960
01:59:44.969 --> 01:59:47.600
of what your life is all about.

2961
01:59:47.600 --> 01:59:50.930
And I'm excited for the possibility of this new TV show.

2962
01:59:50.930 --> 01:59:54.610
And I feel like this is a inflection point in your life,

2963
01:59:54.610 --> 01:59:56.000
and I would just encourage you

2964
01:59:56.000 --> 01:59:57.500
to continue to tell your story

2965
01:59:57.500 --> 02:00:01.110
and to do it with that level of humility and vulnerability

2966
02:00:01.110 --> 02:00:04.030
that you did today cause I think it's really powerful.

2967
02:00:04.030 --> 02:00:07.452
And I think it has the potential to help a lot of people.

2968
02:00:07.452 --> 02:00:08.780
Thanks a million for having me, Rich.

2969
